<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan's CPC sells June fuel oil at below $100/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan's CPC sells June fuel oil at below $100/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state oil company, Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has awarded its tender to sell June high sulphur fuel oil at under $100 per tonne on a free-on-board (fob) basis, a company official said on Friday.</p>
<p>The tender which closed April 24 and was valid for a day, offered the 30,000-tonne cargo loading between June 27-31 from Kaohsiung.</p>
<p>In its previous tender, CPC sold a 30,000 tonne cargo for delivery May 16-25 at $98 per tonne fob.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-870-3082)</p>
